(DocuMind Research Paper: Advances in Retrieval-Augmented Generation) '
(Author: AI Systems Lab \(September 2026\)) '
() '
(Abstract:) '
(Retrieval-Augmented Generation \(RAG\) significantly reduces factual hallucinations) '
(in large language models by grounding output in domain-specific corpus excerpts.) '
(In this work, we demonstrate that chunking with 700 characters and 120 character) '
(sliding-window overlap preserves semantic continuity across complex paragraphs.) '
(Experiments indicate an accuracy boost from 64.2% to 91.8% on factual benchmarks.) '
() '
(Section 1: Architecture & Page Grounding) '
(Standard LLMs often suffer from catastrophic forgetting and temporal cutoff.) '
(By binding page numbers and chunk offsets directly to vector embeddings,) '
(the inference engine provides users with verifiable citations for all factual claims.) '
ET
endstream
endobj
